    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a45">

                <pb facs="0296" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg224"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 44 in No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Datvson to Mr. Lowell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Cork</hi>
                                (<hi rendition="#italic">Queenstown</hi>)</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1882-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 18, 1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy of a
                    letter received to-day from Mr. Michael Hart. I also send copy of a second
                    letter, which, I presume, is intended as a supplement to the first.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. B. DAWSON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Deputy and
                            Vice-Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
